{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "025U", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0007": "$$\nh_f : h_X \\longrightarrow h_Y\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-schemes-gives-representable-transformation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6277c3c74309bde876cdc188956a4ea7197b25fc64e05aa2d97dc9e5e2adef87", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62585258fb1c0f4629c3b86544deb7ccfcb4a0809d8d274d4754259479a89f0d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002> and let\n<MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> be objects of <MATH_0005>.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a morphism of schemes.\nThen\n<MATH_0007>\nis a representable transformation of functors.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f9afe9f1f04d45cbb2bb1145c2026dfa7ef40f7771d9191ef5da57ae5c3eb2a0", "unit_id": "tag:02W9:statement"}
